ey, and new items to add that I hadn’t even considered. The service basically paid for itself! Her knowledge of baby items is invaluable, and her service made me feel so much more confident in my choices.\n\nBridget\n\nImage\n\nI loved everything!! Katie was very efficient. As soon as she got me in, she started working on my list and I got the email with the updates very quickly. The updated list had everything I needed for my family situation and I have actually been changing/purchasing the products. I loved that she checked in on me after a few days so I would actually start changing my registry, because it was something that I kept putting off.\n\nPaula\n\nImage\n\nKatie was a big help in thinking about our current lifestyle, what we were going to get as hand-me-downs, and things that you just don't think about as a first time parent, and how all those things impacted what we actually needed for baby. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUltrasound Registry Review - Pass Your ARDMS Ultrasound Registry. SPI Physics Review, Adult Echocardiography Registry Review, Pediatric Echocardiography Registry Review, Vascular Ultrasound Review, Ultrasound Registry Review (https://www.allaboutultrasound.com/pass-guarantee.html)\nciteturn79search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; \n\n## Pass Guarantee\n\n | \n\nImage: Picture\n\nAt All About Ultrasound | iHeartEcho, we strive to offer Ultrasound Registry Review with results! we stand behind the services we offer and are proud to offer our PASS GUARANTEE.\nIf for any reason, you have subscribed to BOTH our registry review course AND our registry review quiz (if course and standalone quiz is purchased without a bundle - the quiz must have been subscribed to for a minimum of 3 months) and have failed your ARDMS® or CCI® ultrasound registry exam, we will gladly give you access to the same registered course for FREE until you pass. Yes, you read that right, for FREE!\nThere are some terms and conditions that apply:\n1. Registry Review Quiz subscription (or bundle) paid for a minimum of three consecutive months. Please note this does NOT apply to a stand alone quiz subscriptions and must be combined with the course.\n2. Registry Review Course & Quiz must have been accessed with regular use during the subscription period and must have been completed in it's entirety.\n3. Registry Review Test & Learn Quiz must have been accessed and completed with a minimum of ten successful PASS attempts.  \n4. Registry Review Course must have been completed in its entirety with all course modules and videos reviewed and completed.\n5. Request for PASS GUARANTEE ACCESS must be submitted by email to [email protected] within 1 month of the end of the paid Registry Review Course subscription with copies of applicable ARDMS® or CCI®  FAILED registry results. \n\n## Ultrasound Registry Review Simplified\nPass Your ARDMS® & CCI®\n​Ultrasound Registry Exam!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFAQ's (https://www.kidscentraltn.net/humanservices/for-families/child-care-services/background-checks-for-child-care-employees/faq-s.html)\nciteturn79search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; \n\n_______________________________________________________________________________________________________\n\n36. Can I print the disclosure form and out of State forms to use later? Do these forms get updates?\n\nForms are regularly updated. Visit the Child Care Out of State Registry Check web page, then in the middle of the screen there is a box to select the state, below that box, you will see the blue link to the Child Care Criminal/Juvenile History & State Registry Review Disclosure Form, once you have selected and printed this disclosure form, go to the box and select the applicable State, once you have selected the State, then there will be a link or links, in blue, to the form(s) that you need to print, and complete for that State. Please make sure to read and follow directions on our website and on the forms, except never send out of State forms to a State other than Tennessee (*California is the one exception, and the applicant must mail their California form directly to California and send a copy to our office with proof of mailing to California), all forms need to be submitted, to our office, for each applicant, all together at least one day after the applicants fingerprints have been completed.\n\n37. What do I need to do if I have a charge and it has been dismissed or expunged?\n\nPlease send the court documents that show the charge information, including the date of the charge and the charge status being dismissed or expunged to our office email: ccbackground.dhs@tn.gov or fax: +1615-532-9956.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nResources for Florida Nurse Registries | NRC (https://nurseregistryconsultant.com/resources/)\nciteturn79search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 weeks ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; \n\nResources\n\n# Straight answers for Florida nurse registries\n\nPractical articles on licensing, AHCA surveys, and running a nurse registry the right way, written by Scott Strachan, RN, BSN, who has run a licensed Florida nurse registry since 2007.\n\nThe Path to Licensure The Nurse Registry Podcast AHCA & State Contacts Helpful Links Report a Provider to AHCA Free Companion Care Guide\n\n## Articles (11)\n\nOctober 13, 2026\n\n### CEMP Deemed Deficient? What Florida Nurse Registries Need to Know About the 30-Day Revision Deadline\n\nFlorida nurse registry CEMP deemed deficient in the DOH portal? The 30-day revision deadline is in statute. What it means and what to do next.\n\nRead article →\n\nOctober 8, 2026\n\n### Buying Cheap Nurse Registry Policies and Forms? You May Get Exactly What You Paid For\n\nMany Florida nurse registry policy manuals and forms call caregivers employees. That can pass AHCA and still create DOL and IRS misclass